    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Kyle Tucker** (74.09). **Gunnar Henderson** is our primary engine against Warren, benefiting from a massive 16% park factor boost and favorable dynamic platoon splits, while **Kyle Tucker** finds himself in an ideal environment against Freeland despite the lower batting order spot. The middle-infield pairing of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jackson Merrill** (73.43) also provides elite daily efficiency, both taking advantage of soft 4.90+ xERA matchups against Bassitt and Stock, respectively. With **Andy Pages** (72.37) slotting into the two-hole against a lefty, we have effectively weaponized the favorable park factors to maximize our run and RBI potential.\n\nStrategic bench management remains focused on our aggressive SB threshold. **Wade Meckler** (37.55) was the most difficult exclusion today; while his leadoff position and platoon advantage suggested a potential start, the severe SP skill penalty against Pecko dropped him below our 40.0 floor, signaling a day of rest to conserve our cap. We are also monitoring the void left by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jordan Westburg**, whose IL statuses continue to limit our ceiling. While **Sam Antonacci** (61.82) earns the start due to his leadoff potential and favorable platoon, we must remain wary of the 53% hold rate against **Miguel Vargas** (52.38) and the overall risk inherent in relying on dynamic platoon projections for players like **Liam Hicks** (54.32) and **Coby Mayo** (53.00), who face tougher arms than our top-tier performers. Keep a close eye on any late-inning defensive switches for **Dominic Smith** (51.37) if the game script shifts against the Rays, as his platoon advantage is the primary driver of his marginal score.",
